text:
maya: Heads up — customer hit duplicated side-effects after a short 429 storm. Two identical POSTs ~170ms apart.
rui: Did they include Idempotency-Key?
maya: Yes for the normal path but not for the streaming helper in their app.
toni: Classic SDK parity hole. Node/Go helpers attach idempotency in streaming; their Python sampleapp does not.
maya: Also traces show client retried immediately on 429 while a token refresh was happening. Refresh start at 10:41:12.120, retry at 10:41:12.290.
devon: So race = missing idempotency + immediate retry during refresh.
ops-bot: Created ticket DX-4609: "streaming helper parity + refresh jitter guard".
rui: Short term mitigation to share with customer: 1) enable server-side idempotency enforcement, 2) apply client debounce during refresh (150-350ms), 3) upgrade SDKs when patches are out.
toni: Proposed client pattern (JS snippet) to include in sampleapp and docs:
```js
// simple refresh guard + jittered retry
let refreshActive = false;
async function send(req) {
  if (refreshActive) await sleep(randInt(150, 350));
  try { return await fetch(req); }
  catch (e) {
    if (is429(e)) return retryWithExpBackoff(req); throw e;
  }
}
async function refreshToken() { refreshActive = true; await doRefresh(); refreshActive = false }
```
maya: Agree. Also make SDKs attach Idempotency-Key by default for helpers that perform side-effects. Document server requirement: key only helps if server deduplicates.
devon: Telemetry: emit a metric retry.during_refresh with tags {sdk, route, client_id} and a log event when a replay happens with an idempotency-key mismatch. That will let Console owners catch this pattern early.
rui: Add opt-in config flag client.safe_replay = true to enable the guard and idempotency assertions; default false to avoid added latency for low-risk apps.
toni: I'll own Node+Go SDK changes. Maya, can you take Python sampleapp + docs? Devon will add telemetry.
maya: Will do. I'll also add a dev-mode assert in samples that fails if a side-effect POST lacks Idempotency-Key.
ops-bot: PRs opened: node-sdk#611, go-sdk#405, python-samples#89. CI queued at https://ci.internal/dx/611.
devon: For rollout, plan: patch sampleapps + Node/Go helpers this sprint, Python samples and docs next. We'll monitor retry.during_refresh for 48h after rollout.
maya: I'll draft the customer response with remediation steps and link the PRs. Template: 1) enforce idempotency server-side 2) apply client debounce around refresh 3) enable retry telemetry 4) file incident if duplicates persist.
rui: One more: recommend clients use idempotency keys derived from a stable request fingerprint rather than timestamps so retries land on the same key. Add that to docs.
toni: Noted. Let's keep this small and ship fast. :thumbsup:
ops-bot: Incident record dup-replay-2026-09-22 created.
